<h1>EmailNative ⚡ Product Manual & Operations Guide</h1>
<div class="tagline">The Next-Generation Local-First Multi-Domain Email Workstation with Cloudflare, Resend, and DeepSeek-R1 AI</div>

<div class="highlight-box">
  <strong>Executive Value Summary:</strong> EmailNative completely replaces expensive commercial email suites ($6–$12 per user/domain monthly). By synergizing <strong>Cloudflare Email Routing</strong> (unlimited free inbound with wildcard catch-all), <strong>Resend API</strong> (3,000 free monthly outbound emails with DKIM/SPF anti-spam authentication), and local-first client storage, users can manage 10, 50, or 100+ domains with zero monthly server costs and zero data leak risks.
</div>

<h2>1. Comparative Analysis: Traditional Business Email vs EmailNative</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Dimension</th>
      <th>Traditional Suites (Google / M365)</th>
      <th>EmailNative Open-Source Workspace</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Monthly Cost (10 Domains)</strong></td>
      <td><strong>$60 – $120 / month</strong> (charges per user & domain)</td>
      <td><strong>$0 / Lifetime Free</strong> (leverages generous free tiers)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Aliases & Prefixes</strong></td>
      <td>Manual configuration required, strict quota limits</td>
      <td><strong>Unlimited Dynamic Catch-All</strong> (receives on any prefix)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Data Privacy & Keys</strong></td>
      <td>Stored on cloud vendor servers</td>
      <td><strong>Local-First & Zero Server Relay</strong> (Keys stay on device)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>AI Intelligence</strong></td>
      <td>Basic spam scoring</td>
      <td><strong>Native DeepSeek-R1</strong> long reasoning chains, OTP extraction</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Multi-Domain Switching</strong></td>
      <td>Requires multiple browser logins and tab switching</td>
      <td><strong>Unified native workspace</strong> with sub-millisecond switching</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>2. Complete Architecture & Zero-Server Security Model</h2>
<p>
  EmailNative strictly implements a <strong>Local-First Zero-Server Relay</strong> design. All API keys (Cloudflare Token, Resend API Key, DeepSeek API Key) and downloaded email bodies are saved exclusively within your local device’s secure Keychain / LocalStorage. No third-party or proprietary intermediary servers ever touch your communication data.
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Inbound Pipeline:</strong> Cloudflare Email Routing acts as high-throughput mail exchanger (MX), captures emails across any custom domain, triggers an edge Worker to parse MIME content, and stores records in Cloudflare D1.</li>
  <li><strong>Outbound Pipeline:</strong> When you send a reply or compose a new email, the client sends directly to Resend's TLS-encrypted API using your private API key, signing messages with authentic DKIM cryptographic signatures.</li>
  <li><strong>Cognitive AI Pipeline:</strong> When you request AI analysis on an email, the client sends prompts directly to DeepSeek's official endpoint, streaming reasoning chains (<code>&lt;think&gt;</code>) directly to your viewport.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Step-by-Step Setup Guide</h2>

<h3>Step 1: Cloudflare Email Routing Configuration</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Log in to the Cloudflare Dashboard and select your domain name.</li>
  <li>Navigate to <strong>Email &rarr; Email Routing</strong> and click <strong>Enable Email Routing</strong>.</li>
  <li>Ensure the MX and basic SPF records are verified:</li>
</ol>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Type</th>
      <th>Name</th>
      <th>Target / Value</th>
      <th>Priority</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>MX</td>
      <td>@</td>
      <td>isaac.mx.cloudflare.net</td>
      <td>13</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>MX</td>
      <td>@</td>
      <td>linda.mx.cloudflare.net</td>
      <td>57</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>MX</td>
      <td>@</td>
      <td>amir.mx.cloudflare.net</td>
      <td>98</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>TXT</td>
      <td>@</td>
      <td>v=spf1 include:_spf.mx.cloudflare.net include:resend.com ~all</td>
      <td>-</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>TXT</td>
      <td>_dmarc</td>
      <td>v=DMARC1; p=none;</td>
      <td>-</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Step 2: Cloudflare Email Inbound Worker & D1 Database</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Create a new Cloudflare Worker (e.g., <code>emailnative-gateway</code>).</li>
  <li>Go to Worker <strong>Settings &rarr; Bindings</strong>, and create a D1 database binding named exactly <code>DB</code> (capital letters).</li>
  <li>Under <strong>Variables</strong>, add an Environment Variable named <code>ADMIN_TOKEN</code> with a secure secret password.</li>
  <li>Copy and deploy the production code from <code>cloudflare/worker.js</code>.</li>
  <li>In <strong>Email Routing &rarr; Routing Rules</strong>, set the <strong>Catch-all rule</strong> action to <strong>Send to Worker</strong>, selecting your gateway worker.</li>
</ol>

<h3>Step 3: Resend Outbound Channel Setup</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Sign up for a free account at <a href="https://resend.com">resend.com</a>.</li>
  <li>Add your domain and follow the instructions to add the DKIM CNAME records in Cloudflare DNS (ensure proxy status is <strong>DNS Only</strong> / grey cloud).</li>
  <li>Generate a Sending API Key and paste it into EmailNative <strong>Settings &rarr; Outbound</strong>.</li>
</ol>

<h2>4. DeepSeek-R1 AI Intelligence & Cost Protection</h2>
<div class="highlight-box">
  <strong>Zero Token Waste Philosophy:</strong> EmailNative does not perform automated background token burning on incoming junk or low-value mail. All AI cognitive tasks run purely on-demand, giving the operator 100% financial control.
</div>

<h3>4.1 On-Demand AI Analysis</h3>
<p>
  When reviewing a customer recommendation, feature inquiry, or critical communication, click the <strong>AI Analysis</strong> button. DeepSeek-R1 will unpack the underlying intent, grade customer sentiment, assess urgency, and draft an appropriate reply matching the domain's brand persona.
</p>

<h3>4.2 Budget Protection & Circuit Breakers</h3>
<p>
  In <strong>Settings &rarr; Cost Safeguards</strong>, you can define:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Max Cost Per Run:</strong> Protects against anomalous oversized emails from consuming excessive context tokens.</li>
  <li><strong>Daily Budget Limit:</strong> When cumulative daily expenditure reaches your specified watermark, automated analysis halts immediately to protect your bank balance.</li>
  <li><strong>Emergency Stop Button:</strong> At any point during a reasoning stream, you can click Emergency Stop to cancel network requests and freeze token calculation.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. One-Click DNS & Deliverability Health Inspector</h2>
<p>
  To prevent legitimate outgoing business emails from ending up in spam folders, EmailNative features an integrated DNS Inspector:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>MX Verification:</strong> Ensures that incoming mail servers are configured and responsive.</li>
  <li><strong>SPF Policy Check:</strong> Verifies that Resend's sending IPs are authorized in your domain's TXT record.</li>
  <li><strong>DKIM Public Key Validation:</strong> Confirms public key cryptographic signature records exist.</li>
  <li><strong>DMARC Alignment:</strong> Validates domain authentication policies.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Keyboard Shortcuts Quick Reference</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Shortcut</th>
      <th>Action</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="kbd">Cmd</span> + <span class="kbd">N</span></td>
      <td>Compose New Email</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="kbd">Cmd</span> + <span class="kbd">,</span></td>
      <td>Open System Settings</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="kbd">Cmd</span> + <span class="kbd">R</span></td>
      <td>Sync Inbound Mail from Cloudflare</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="kbd">Cmd</span> + <span class="kbd">T</span></td>
      <td>Toggle Theme (Dark Glass / Pure Light)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="kbd">Esc</span></td>
      <td>Close Modal / Inspector / Drawer</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

